# Myna - optional settings read at start-up.
# Copy this file to ".env" and remove the "#" in front of what you want to change.
# Everyday settings (API key, language, voice, notifications, ...) are NOT here:
# set those in the web console, they are saved under the data folder.

# --- Where the agent listens -------------------------------------------------
# Default: this computer only. To open the web console from other devices on
# your network set AGENT_HOST=0.0.0.0 and ALSO set both tokens below.
#AGENT_HOST=127.0.0.1
#AGENT_PORT=8787

# Password for the web console and its API (send as ?token=... or
# "Authorization: Bearer ..."). Leave empty only when AGENT_HOST is 127.0.0.1.
#CALLS_UI_TOKEN=

# Phones that connect over Wi-Fi must use ws://<this-pc>:8787/ws?token=<this>.
# Phones on USB do not need it.
#DEVICE_TOKEN=

# Address of the web console as you reach it, for links in notifications.
# Empty: http://<MDNS_NAME>.local:8787 (or this computer's network address)
# when AGENT_HOST opens the console to your network; in Docker set it yourself.
#PUBLIC_URL=http://192.168.1.20:8787

# Name on your network: with AGENT_HOST=0.0.0.0, phones and computers on the
# same network open the web console at http://myna.local:8787 (when this
# computer lets the agent answer the name). off, 0, none or false = off
# (write "off": on Windows an empty value counts as not set).
# On a VPN that sends all traffic through the tunnel, set AGENT_HOST to this
# computer's LAN IP (e.g. 192.168.1.20) so the name and links use it.
#MDNS_NAME=myna

# --- Start script -------------------------------------------------------------
# 1 = do not put the "Myna Console" shortcut to the web console on the desktop.
#MYNA_NO_SHORTCUT=1

# --- Data ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Call records, recordings and settings. Default: ./data/calls
#CALLS_DATA_DIR=
# Keep calls and recordings this many days.
#CALLS_RETENTION_DAYS=7

# --- Phones on USB ------------------------------------------------------------
# The agent keeps "adb reverse" up and starts the phone app by itself.
# off = you do that yourself (phones on Wi-Fi, or another computer has the phones).
#USB_BRIDGE=on
# Full path to adb when several are installed (mixing adb versions drops phones).
#ADB_BIN=
# Only these phones (serials from "adb devices", comma separated). Default: all.
#ADB_SERIALS=

# --- First-run defaults (the web console overrides them) ----------------------
#GEMINI_API_KEY=
#APP_LANGUAGE=en
#OWNER_NAME=
#ANSWER_STYLE=assistant

# --- Logging ------------------------------------------------------------------
#RUST_LOG=agent=info
